[?2004l=== USTAR ===
ustar member header is 512 bytes. name occupies bytes 0-99. size octal occupies 124-135 (the slice end is 136). typeflag sits at 156: regular file uses ASCII 0 (the byte that Python writes as b"0"). Payload follows the header and is padded to 512.

walk_sig is hashlib.sha256 hex of regular-file names joined by newline in apply order (SHA-256). Length is 64. Alphabet is 0123456789abcdef.

A quarry of truncated bytes or a non-ustar stream such as not-an-archive returns nonzero. A ledger filled with xxxx is junk and quarry must rebuild members.idx from the sealed kith.

python3 -c import hashlib,sys; print(hashlib.sha256(sys.stdin.buffer.read()).hexdigest())
=== DESK ===
Desk JSON keys: timezone, cluster, log_events, member_count, source_kith, walk_sig.

sys.conf uses key=value lines. timezone and cluster come from the sys.conf payload the mill applies. log_events is the lexicographically sorted unique event strings from every app.log payload. member_count is the integer of regular-file payloads applied. source_kith is the archive basename.

A brief archive copied to /tmp/kestrel.kith sits outside /app/sealwell. The sealed original also lives at /app/seed/sealwell/kestrel.kith.
=== APPLY ===
operator note: APPLY
=== SEAL ===
cordpit notes: two brief processes on one sealed kith must parse to one object. Paths outside sealwell fail.
=== TREE ===
idxmill
overlaypit
logbag
siltcli
ustarwalk
cfgbag
offseturn
paxcue
pidhash
keeppit
